                                <li>Statement of Qualifications - <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt;">The Statement of Qualifications (SOQ) is separate from the application and is a narrative discussion of how each candidate&#39;s education, training, experience, and skills meet the qualifications to perform the functions as outlined in the duty statement.&nbsp; The SOQ serves as documentation of each candidate&#39;s ability to present information clearly and concisely in writing.&nbsp; The SOQ will be used in conjunction with the interview results to assist the interview panel in determining the most qualified candidate for the position.&nbsp; If you do not have an expertise in a certain category, indicate this on the SOQ and include examples of similar experience that would demonstrate your ability or potential to perform the specific function. &nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;">SEE SOQ INSTRUCTIONS BELOW&nbsp;</span></p></li>
                            
